cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Political Payola datasets, rankings, or cross-tabulated roll-call and FEC records in academic, journalistic, or policy research, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Political Payola — Verified Multi-Source Civic, Legislative & Public-Health Atlas (1981–2026)"
version: "2.4.0"
date-released: "2026-10-31"
url: "https://politicalpayola.com/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/jjordanjr74-dot/politicalpayola-site"
license: "CC-BY-4.0"
authors:
  - family-names: "Jordan"
    given-names: "Tristan"
    affiliation: "Political Payola Civic Transparency Project (Pueblo, Colorado)"
keywords:
  - "campaign finance"
  - "FEC filings"
  - "119th Congress"
  - "roll-call votes"
  - "state health rankings"
  - "bilingual civic literacy"
  - "WebMCP"
  - "open civic data"
abstract: >-
  Longitudinal, bilingual (EN/ES) public-interest dataset of 5,111 primary-source verified civic,
  medical, academic, and legislative records spanning 1981–2026. Cross-references official federal
  sources (FEC.gov, Congress.gov, CBO, BLS, CDC, Census SAIPE) with peer-reviewed research
  (JAMA Network Open, NEJM, AJPM, KFF, Pew Research Center, NBER, PIIE, Rutgers CAWP) across
  all 50 U.S. states and all 539 members of the 119th Congress.
